# Rust build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
**/mutants.out*/

# Secrets — NEVER commit Bitwarden vault exports or derived files.
# These files contain plaintext passwords, TOTP seeds, and passkey data.
bitwarden_export_*.json                    # `bw export --format json` output
bitwarden_decrypted-export_*.json          # `just backup-vault-decrypted` output
bitwarden_encrypted-export_*.json          # `just backup-vault-encrypted` output
bitwarden_sync_*.json                      # legacy `bw export` / pre-rename snapshots
*.dedup.json                               # `just dedup` deduplicated output
*.dedup.audit.json                         # `just dedup` per-removal audit
*.dedup.trashed.json                       # `just dedup` losers sidecar
*-with-icloud-credentials.json             # `just merge-with-icloud-credentials-csv` merged output
*-with-icloud-credentials.audit.json       # … its audit
*-with-icloud-credentials.trashed.json     # … its losers sidecar
# Local redactor output (bitwarden-redact). The redacted replica still
# contains vault-shape metadata (counts, per-item URI counts, dates) and
# is intended for local reviewer sharing, not commit.
*.redacted.json
*-redacted.json
redacted-*.json
vault/

# Exception: the committed synthetic fixture lives under examples/ and
# uses the `bitwarden_export_<timestamp>.json` filename format. It is
# produced exclusively by tests/fixture.rs::build_curated_fixture() and
# every string it contains is shape-checked by the leak-guard test. The
# `examples_directory_contains_only_fixture` test enforces that this
# is the ONLY file under examples/, so the exception can never be used
# to smuggle in a real export.
!examples/bitwarden_export_*.json
